      "writtenOn": "2025-11-17T20:33:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, the thing that bothers me here is that:\n1. You don\u0027t actually care about the alignment of the struct, you care about the alignment of `apiakey_lo`/`apiakey_hi` pairs for the 128-bit wide `stp`\n2. It implicitly depends on C layout rules. These are static, so it\u0027s safe, but you\u0027re relying on how C says you have to lay out struct fields rather than having direct restrictions on how they\u0027re laid out.\n\nI don\u0027t know that we can do a ton better though if you think they make most sense as separate registers.",
